PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The deliberation has reached complete consensus across all colleagues that $\kappa = -(\tau_u + \tau_v)\left(\mu + \frac{\rho}{\phi}\right) = -\frac{\tau_u + \tau_v}{\phi}(\phi \mu + \rho)$. Setting the expected synaptic weight drift $\langle \dot{w}_k \rangle = 0$ at steady state and isolating the critical correlation in $c^* = \frac{\kappa S - 1}{S - 1}$ directly yields this expression. Because the plasticity rule uses an additive offset $\rho$, net baseline depression requires $\rho < -\phi \mu < 0$, making $\kappa$ strictly positive and physically consistent. For future rounds, we will present the primary algebraic forms alongside each other to cover all standard literature conventions.
}

